// App manifest for the hub app — a name → real-ESM-import map (the
// synthetic-view import map). Modeled on the deck-conformance manifest.
//
// SUI stays ignorant of what these names MEAN: `route`/`navigate` are
// deck/app concepts (the URL handle + imperative navigation behind the
// view-host), not SUI ones. This map is what REPLACES the reserved-word
// BUILTINS/ambient-ctx mechanism — composition by real import, type-checked
// by tsgo/tsc, the compiler unaware that "route" or "navigate" exist.
//
// `construct: true` means the import is a factory (`route()` → RouteSignals),
// so the synthetic controller emits `const route = route()`. `navigate` is a
// plain function value (construct omitted → false).
//
// The home route (`/`) reads only its authored `name` signal, so it imports
// none of these — the per-view resolver imports only the names a view
// actually references. They are declared here because they are the standard
// view-host handles every hub route may use.
{
  "clients": {
    "route": { "from": "@ship/deck/route", "import": "route", "construct": true },
    "navigate": { "from": "@ship/deck/route", "import": "navigate" }
  }
}
